  "review": "# Independent native log review\n\nRead-only review of root native-script-logs diff on91b6952. No source edits or Cargo. The initial logging parser used rquickjs0.14 CString::as_str on arbitrary guest strings. That API calls from_utf8_unchecked; pinned QuickJS JS_ToCStringLen2 preserves lone UTF16 surrogates, and utf8_encode emits their invalid UTF8 byte sequences. log(\"\\\\uD800\") or a lone-surrogate level could therefore violate Rust str invariants. The earlier timer ASCII parser shared this defect.\n\nCorrective delta inspected: both paths use CString only for bounded byte-length preflight, then drop it and invoke the original immutable rquickjs String::to_string checked conversion. No unchecked string view or new unsafe code remains. New high/low/mixed-surrogate refusal cases test transactional rejection in logs and timers; ordinary valid-pair emoji coverage is preserved. Parent runs the final test/Clippy chain36975 and patches the pending timer PR before merge.\n\nNo remaining blocker found in reviewed source. Primitive-only argument conversion invokes no guest coercion; per-tick failure is latched even when guest catches the exception. Logging is revoked before diagnostics and numeric validation. Records publish only after detached numeric/structural acceptance, and failed sessions expose none through their public observers. Prior function capabilities never reactivate. Prefix count/UTF8-byte bounds and saturating drop counts remain finite; final player output serializes once, not per tick. Native/game wrappers retain terminal output-hiding semantics after backend/host failure. Official rquickjs Flat supplies all eight guest arguments without a manual ABI.\n\nActual-process proof extension retains baseline Unicode/tick/level checks on existing success processes and adds retained-history count/byte controls plus four no-output invalid-update controls. These sources were inspected, not independently executed in this review. QuickJS-only scope remains explicit; no Wasm logging ABI, phone performance or phase gate is approved.\n\nCorrected hashes:\n- `crates/incant_script/src/logging.rs`: `03bb5a68c9f4d151d336aaa5e9c5e76a12beb6b7628186e3ce3d47b3c0bfa19a`\n- `crates/incant_script/src/log_tests.rs`: `0d2cc53188097a722396ef6c38602b3979c2641694b078a6d7d24ef8ab13ff60`\n- `crates/incant_script/src/lib.rs`: `ce7317f8c6ac188e13f283431aa61e10262223d6620a7dd33246dc401344fa2d`\n- `crates/incant_script/src/timers.rs`: `fcad95765d4229909facc70149f984584eee8bd3b808960dab3723c17ed352d0`\n- `crates/incant_script/src/timer_tests.rs`: `057f655888c8e6ccc3dd9054113a026ee04ad2c8315259d6acadd41e13870ff7`\n- `crates/incant_game_runtime/src/core.rs`: `2ab19f1c78eb5b6dbe8bde72d0a098314cfbc42e50d92feb0b5004b487804ace`\n- `crates/incant_game_player/src/session.rs`: `c3a3751f79e8d5688c23620258a089a672ac02d66c50c382199d2aa3b6548282`\n- `crates/incant_game_player/src/main.rs`: `2143af678d557f012810e390db243649ec3bf158d0221ec5d355112b392fee8a`\n- `sdk/ts/src/native.d.ts`: `a3e3f12dc16ce8dd1a7b7222e576b873e8cb5692958ed34610e7204dbe3fded6`\n- `tools/native_logs.py`: `2a2549a56959d359ad54161e05948e8569329db57724ee4cf4f2d7aa8e206b76`\n- `tools/probes/native-game.py`: `87da45c972ded58ca1c7989d4127889be0862c1cfe293912f6625e19cfb7450d`\n",
